The image shows diced cooked chicken breast pieces in a large steel mixing bowl. The bowl looks about 25-30 cm across, so the pile of chicken covers roughly 10 cm by 9 cm. The pieces are about 2 cm each, and I count roughly 40 of them. Each piece is around 2x2x1.5 cm, or about 6 cm³, which is about 6 g. That gives roughly 40 × 5 g = 200 g, but the pieces are thin and the layer is sparse, so I'll lower it to about 100 g.

Cooked chicken breast is about 165 kcal per 100 g, so 100 g comes to about 165 kcal.

